{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036883-third-name","id":1036883,"title":"Third name?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-23T15:57:02-08:00","id":1036883,"title":"Third name?","content":"I'm tired, so maybe I'm forgetting something really obvious. However, I've to ask: Do mages use a third name?<br /> <br /> Your True/Birth/Slave Name has a sympathetic connection to you that is quite strong, it is worth concealing. Your Shadow Name is a secret. 'Calling out a Shadow Name in mixed company is a considerable faux pas depending on where and when. It\u2019s revealing a secret, frankly, like shouting a lover\u2019s favorite sexual position in the middle of family dinner.' P.292<br /> <br /> So if one gives others a way to sink their claws into you, and the other is on a par with your sexual preference (I'm kidding; it is secretive though), then would Mages not have a Noble Lie Name that they can use in public and for reference but which is weakened as a connection by its nature as a mask. That way, your friend can say 'Why not invite Jim?' without risking your existence.<br /> <br /> Again, tired, might be missing something but...yeah, what's up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:12:39-08:00","id":1036893,"title":"","content":"Alternate Identity is on pg. 105 of the 2e core.<br /> <br /> It's not that vital, but it's not unreasonable either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:17:16-08:00","id":1036896,"title":"","content":"One of my mage characters does precisely that. His sympathetic name's Timothy Kemp, but goes by the alias Garrick Royce in public, and by Phoenix among mages.<br /> <br /> I'd say given the circumstances, this is inevitably a common practice. So if you're missing something, then I'm missing something, too. And I'm not tired, so I suspect that your thinking isn't being impaired, at least with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:33:29-08:00","id":1036903,"title":"","content":"Thats what we did in our first campaing of Mage back in 1st ED, too - our Guardians loved shuffling newly Awakened around the country, giving them new identities and new lives in far away cities, while covering their tracks and maintaining a facade for your family to believe in, so you can call and pretend you really moved due to awesome job opportunity. <br /> Now we use much smaller scale consilia and dropped down politicking considerably, and with it the oppressive cold war, so Mages don't need it as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:57:40-08:00","id":1036914,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thanks for the replies.<br /> <br /> So, if I make a Guardian, I face having four names at least: True, Shadow, Alternative, and Mask. Mages really do embody mystery. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:20:40-08:00","id":1036926,"title":"","content":"Uhhh... True Name is a different thing than what 1e called Real Name and 2e calls Sympathetic Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T00:20:34-08:00","id":1037074,"title":"","content":"True Name is your <i>new</i> Name given by Archmaster of Space that <u>overwritten</u> your Sympathy Name. If your 'Slave' Name was Bob Ericson, and given True Name of Merlin, Sympathy works on you only on Merlin, not Bob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}